                'en' => 'On Sunday 14 August 1898 an overnight stopping train that had left Paris at 11.16 pm derailed at about 4.15 am at the place called Lieu Galant, in the commune of Saint-Jacques (Calvados), between Saint-Mards-de-Fresne and Lisieux, on the Paris - Caen - Cherbourg line. The train, crowded on the eve of the 15 August long weekend, had two vans and about nineteen coaches, hauled by two locomotives.',
